# Adversarial case, ratified by the author 2026-08-04.
# Guards panel 007: there is NO continuation at bracket depth zero. A line
# ending in `+` gets no terminator, so the next line is read as part of the
# same expression — and an indented line there is a block, not a continuation.
#
# Correction, 2026-09-28 (panel 181, provisional): the first claim above was
# false at the statement's own margin, where `total = 1 +` over `2` compiled
# and ran until this date, as the second sentence says of the line after `+`
# (defect 116); this case tested only the deeper line, refused as a block.
# Both margins are one refusal now, of the line end at the `+`, which is
# where the annotation and the `.expected` moved from the `2`:
# `continuation_outside_brackets` (`selfhost/open_line.hero`).
function main()
    #~v continuation_outside_brackets
    total = 1 +
        2
